<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Wildfires, heatwaves threaten global air quality and health, UN warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e217034cd9225d84a9041e917e207f6b1829d8d821ff5495c08bf0696cee012e</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T04:16:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20260907-wildfires-heatwaves-global-air-quality-health-un--1a101659d339.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20260907-wildfires-heatwaves-global-air-quality-health-un" /><summary type="html">Wildfires and heatwaves are threatening global efforts to improve air quality and protect human health, the World Meteorological Organisation said on Monday. The UN agency warned that increasingly severe fires are raising exposure to toxic PM2.5 pollution, even as regulations have reduced industrial and transport emissions in Europe and North America.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East Live: Israel army orders evacuation of zone in south Lebanon ahead of strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed563a0fe2e4d84f2567b0ba0a5b835fab359c1a8e71983397a24fa35c97cdd6</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T01:13:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes--2806097dc20d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes" /><summary type="html">The Israeli army demanded early Monday that residents of Deir Zahrani in southern Lebanon leave a specific zone ahead of strikes against Iran-backed Hezbollah. Hezbollah's Al-Manar television channel later reported Israeli airstrikes on Deir Zahrani. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys bring ‘more effective’ Ukraine peace proposals to Kyiv, official says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4038652521024166d5f0270ee942cd653ff23756a11f64b40a3e8c4d42778683</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv--37419914ba3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv" /><summary type="html">US envoys brought new, “more effective” proposals to Kyiv aimed at ending the war with Russia, a senior Ukrainian presidential official said on Sunday. President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner described talks positively but announced no breakthrough, as Zelensky warned fighting could continue into winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU to boost Greenland investment amid Trump annexation claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40d9d77461710781d10b11d1daba8812b7b831e63a726749822ba7cfdd3ea952</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation--2b5a527b0c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is expected to announce increased EU investment in Greenland on Monday, including in critical minerals, satellite communications and renewable energy. Her two-day visit signals support for Greenland and Denmark amid US President Donald Trump’s push for American control of the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Amazon cargo plane crashes at Miami airport, killing at least five</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f7c2d983aa6bc684e6cd9cbfdc27e5728ad58573006309494c408fe971d83f8</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:59:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260906-amazon-cargo-plane-crashes-miami-airport-killing-at-least-five--0db603298e6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260906-amazon-cargo-plane-crashes-miami-airport-killing-at-least-five" /><summary type="html">At least five people were killed and five injured after an Amazon cargo plane overshot the runway at Miami International Airport on Sunday and crashed into several vehicles, officials said. Miami Sheriff Rosie Cordero-Stutz said there was “no apparent threat to public safety” following the crash.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>"Ready to talk": German far-right celebrates victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce8057a8f69df8280e13561e015241bfe17a1432a16afa4e93b8dc4cb7c2c24c</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T17:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory--e252fd4fc28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory" /><summary type="html">“Everything is possible” is the election campaign slogan of the far-right Alternative for Germany, the leader in Saxony-Anhalt, where the polls have just closed. It talks of a seminal moment for the country. Ulrich Siegmund, who has been polling in pole position to become the state leader, knows he has history in his grasp.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Germany’s far-right AfD landslide winner in key Saxony-Anhalt vote, early results suggest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2247509069d68f145c1269de6b646e5865b77ff1bc98f6985b985d94b38bb48</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:18:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism--5b3d7165d920.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s far-right AfD landslide winner in key Saxony-Anhalt vote, early results suggest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:102cec363ca5d1e9a6327501afab438e840dbc68d997d9e81f52ce515b384b10</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest--ba93eb6e2f1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest" /><summary type="html">Germany’s far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party headed towards a landslide victory in state ​elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, with 44.5 percent of the vote, early results showed. But despite the scale of its projected win, it was not immediately clear whether AfD would be able to form Germany’s first far-right state government since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>AfD could lead "the first far-right state government since the dark days of Nazism"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2907997a8b60d3b7777f6cd0fd613de819a4d391b55724ef282f7eac2d6c8445</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:07:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism--5b3d7165d920.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism" /><summary type="html">Voting is underway in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election. "If the AfD does form a government in Saxony-Anhalt, that would make it the first regional government headed by a far-right party since the end of the Second World War, since the dark days of Nazism", our correspondent Nick Holdsworth explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Deauville Film Festival: What’s your favourite American film?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46640199a10415b1f433c6aac5ac16a26a8ea41e1023a4b7e9b7d9c99bc31fb9</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T15:43:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-deauville-film-festival-what-s-your-favourite-american-film--97122c70df72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-deauville-film-festival-what-s-your-favourite-american-film" /><summary type="html">The United States ranks second in the world in terms of the number of films produced. It produces between 500 and 700 films every year, which is just behind India. The Deauville Film Festival, with its stars, premieres and awards, aims to showcase the very best of what’s being made across the Atlantic. But on the other side of the screen, moviegoers also have their say. What’s your favourite American film? Is it one that shaped your childhood, or a recent discovery? Our reporter Gaëlle Fonseca hit the streets of Deauville to ask that very question.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: What could change in Saxony-Anhalt if the AfD wins?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd18e7d4ade79de0d3652c7e2581b816c4fc5b0a05a95b1a92654f5eb060ec27</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:44:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-what-could-change-in-saxony-anhalt-if-the-afd-wins--06a1a616dfdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-what-could-change-in-saxony-anhalt-if-the-afd-wins" /><summary type="html">Voting began in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election. Recent surveys place the AfD at just over 40%, followed by Merz's Christian Democrats (CDU) at 23%. If the AfD wins, "one of the main things they want to change is the education system. They say they want to reset education," our journalist Shirli Stibon explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Under-fire FIFA boss Infantino to seek re-election despite calls to resign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4084b43a6f060bd8a4ac782afa79118495ba198d04fef1a15c356759e2dad2f3</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260906-under-fire-fifa-boss-infantino-to-seek-re-election-despite-calls-to-resign--24212ecccf92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260906-under-fire-fifa-boss-infantino-to-seek-re-election-despite-calls-to-resign" /><summary type="html">FIFA President Gianni Infantino plans to seek his fourth and final term in next year’s election, despite the outrage sparked by his now-shelved plan to sell stakes in the World Cup to private investors. “Nothing has changed,” a spokesman for football’s governing body confirmed on Sunday, referring to an announcement Infantino made back in April.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Nepal rescue operations, World Nomad Games and Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5af9ce20a2cf84aed17e6e1920477a194d81d9cc10a927d2c20503371749bdcf</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:21:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d0868f737f26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">From the desperate search for workers trapped in the hydropower tunnels buried by the catastrophic flooding in Nepal to crowds of women mourning the victims of a US bombardment of a wedding in southern Iran, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: AfD's Ulrich Siegmund eyes outright majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2274c889c6f155e973c8e7cc1c8d5189b28451ce4daec25108c625d5bb22331</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:07:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-afd-s-ulrich-siegmund-eyes-outright-majority--85bee13ef1d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-afd-s-ulrich-siegmund-eyes-outright-majority" /><summary type="html">Under its 35-year-old lead ​candidate Ulrich Siegmund, the ‌AfD has polled above 40% for months and has a realistic shot at winning an absolute majority if several smaller parties fail ⁠to clear Germany's 5% hurdle to enter parliament.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine-Russia talks: What are the US objectives?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf442955f5595a46040a92f4e3ba1b29096b223662b075b9563ee0e5f99ec6b</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ukraine-russia-talks-what-are-the-us-objectives--e1f34f992a6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ukraine-russia-talks-what-are-the-us-objectives" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Kyiv on Sunday in their first official visit to Ukraine as part of a renewed push for peace, more than 4½ years after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine. We discuss this topic with our guest, John E. Herbst, director of the Eurasia Center at the Atlantic Council.</summary></entry><entry><title>Egyptian TV presenter Sarah Khalifa sentenced to death in drug case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ff480e4e7d2015a73759cddc3c4d3fe37b4d5316a1fd19f4e9133cbd8efbf68</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T13:52:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260906-egyptian-tv-presenter-sarah-khalifa-sentenced-to-death-in-drug-case--a5ffad89f8f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260906-egyptian-tv-presenter-sarah-khalifa-sentenced-to-death-in-drug-case" /><summary type="html">Sarah Khalifa, a well-known Egyptian TV presenter, has been sentenced to death for her involvement in a drug ring, state media reported over the weekend. Eleven others were also convicted in the case and handed a death sentence. Khalifa is best known for her program “Mission Impossible”.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>AI: The future of smart households?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed9103a0be2647642b37028cc066c269b0ab8a9ccfa6d7c02a9711551d96456e</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T13:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ai-the-future-of-smart-households--1a2413209383.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ai-the-future-of-smart-households" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence soon be running our households? Beyond our smartphones, AI is now powering everything from fridges to lawnmowers. The International Household Appliances Fair in Berlin gives us a glimpse into what's next.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Why is the AfD so popular in Saxony-Anhalt?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e5de71107d2dd0a23f6441d8810bc960a7ba63f3f7fc1c63e861e6d48d7848d</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T13:37:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-why-is-the-afd-so-popular-in-saxony-anhalt--c090ff3c9e51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-why-is-the-afd-so-popular-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">Voting began in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election that could see the Alternative for Germany (AfD) become the first far-right party to lead a state government since World War II. We discuss this with our guest, Hans Stark, professor of German studies at Sorbonne University.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's Anak Krakatau eruption halts flights, schools, fishing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3db5bd04dedcb4c0d06e7a56a3ee56e2da431d73b663e64cdab0c283775ab186</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T12:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-indonesia-s-anak-krakatau-eruption-halts-flights-schools-fishing--544357425e2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-indonesia-s-anak-krakatau-eruption-halts-flights-schools-fishing" /><summary type="html">An eruption of Indonesia's Mount Anak Krakatau caused six airports to suspend flight operations on Sunday, affecting hundreds of flights at Jakarta's main airport, after some school activities and fishing were halted.</summary></entry><entry><title>Commemoration held for late Bosnian Serb war criminal Ratko Mladic</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d86c4309712c00f35ff63db83e9ee8171c89ada3b93acac54505cdd3f37cec0</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T12:52:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-commemoration-held-for-late-bosnian-serb-war-criminal-ratko-mladic--a83db4c03493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-commemoration-held-for-late-bosnian-serb-war-criminal-ratko-mladic" /><summary type="html">A commemoration was held Saturday in Belgrade for war criminal Ratko Mladic two days ahead of his burial, attended by dozens of former military personnel, family members and officials.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD clear frontrunner in eastern state vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df9bf2ceb5fb8af0e0a2f0bc03018ec8416111ff458d174d147be773429a96e2</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T11:54:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-clear-frontrunner-in-eastern-state-vote-1--2d672b35c065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-clear-frontrunner-in-eastern-state-vote-1" /><summary type="html">German voters headed to the polls on Sunday for a key regional election in the ex-communist east where the far-right, anti-immigrant, Moscow- and Trump-friendly AfD is expected to secure an easy majority. Our correspondent Nick Holdsworth tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethan Hawke receives the Deauville Talent Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7412e30f4f4e8a4c725402eed1e3f02f753de60ba47e814088d73eea66177d18</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T11:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ethan-hawke-receives-the-deauville-talent-award--c796d27b0398.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ethan-hawke-receives-the-deauville-talent-award" /><summary type="html">Known for starring in Dead Poets Society, the Before trilogy and Boyhood, Hollywood legend Ethan Hawke receives the #Deauville #Talent #Award in recognition of his career spanning nearly 40 years.
 
He also plays the lead role in The Weight, screened at the Opening Ceremony of the 52nd Deauville #American #Film #Festival and due to be released in theaters on September 16. Our reporter Gaëlle Fonseca spoke to him on the red carpet.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Army Secretary Dan Driscoll quits: "What we've seen is almost a factional clash"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcf4a8ad0516aff7f24a4d139a7cb314aa3a3102dddf3659d828ee60e10d3cce</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T11:34:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-us-army-secretary-dan-driscoll-quits-what-we-ve-seen-is-almost-a-factional-clash--91b778356eaf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-us-army-secretary-dan-driscoll-quits-what-we-ve-seen-is-almost-a-factional-clash" /><summary type="html">Amid the US conflict with Iran, Democrats and some Republicans are warning of a leadership void at the top of the US military. That's after the resignation this week of the Army's top civilian official, Army Secretary Dan Driscoll, amid widespread reports of tensions with Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Our guest, Walter Ladwig, associate professor of international relations at King's College London, tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Trump's envoys Witkoff and Kushner arrive in Kyiv after 'substantive' talks with Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70f0a0141a4d5f193c06fda46f341720660bdf9a60e2cd649b72dc4d45a5d03b</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:18:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin--f41091ccbfca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin" /></entry></feed>
